    "payload": {
      "kind": "study",
      "title": "Story pace of gummy worms in zero gravity",
      "authors": [
        "Fictional Orbital Confectionery Group"
      ],
      "journal": "Fictional Journal of Orbital Confectionery",
      "year": 2024,
      "body": "Aboard the spaceship Sugar Comet, twenty fictional groups of gummy worms told the same tale of a marshmallow moon, half with gravity switched on and half floating. Groups with gravity finished in an average of 60 seconds; floating groups finished in 45 seconds. Floating storytellers paused less because nobody had to climb back onto the story rug. The study measured pace only; it did not test what listeners remembered. All results are invented demonstration data. Correction: a timing error had shortened the floating average, which is 45 seconds, not 40."
    }
  },
